SECTION_5_AUDIENCE_INTELLIGENCE
who_they_are: Women (primarily Gen Z/younger Millennial) already identifying with or exploring bohemian personal style — free-spirited, nature-and-travel-drawn, drawn to handmade/artisanal aesthetics. They are searching "boho nails" not because they need a manicure, but because they are confirming that this look matches who they already are or want to be. Many are pre-event (festival, wedding, vacation) planners.
what_they_want_from_this_post: Confirmation that boho is "their" aesthetic, wide visual range across sub-styles (desert, celestial, wedding, dark, festival), and enough specificity (colors, shapes, symbols) to describe the look to a nail tech or replicate at home.
what_frustrates_them: Generic "earthy tones + florals" advice repeated everywhere without genuine differentiation from other earthy aesthetics (cottagecore); scattered, contradictory shape advice; no clear entry point for total beginners who don't know where their "boho" ends and someone else's begins.
top_5_pain_points:
1. Can't tell if they're "boho," "cottagecore," or "fairycore" — genuinely confused by overlapping earthy/nature language across the three
2. Don't know which nail shape/length actually suits boho work vs. generic advice saying "any shape works"
3. Want DIY instructions, not just inspiration photos — most sources are galleries with zero technique
4. Uncertain whether boho nails read as professional/appropriate outside festivals and vacations
5. Overwhelmed by sub-trend fragmentation (desert vs crystal vs dark vs wedding) with no single guide organizing all of it
